# SHACL-closure-only lookup: existence stubs for referential-integrity checks
# (testTopoReferencesExist / testTopoDirectedReferencesExist). This is deliberately a SEPARATE
# file from referenced-objects.ttl (which supplies real geometry to the topo2geojson transform):
# a shaclClosures file is merged into every consuming block's validation graph, so any id in it
# that ALSO carries real geometry collides (as two distinct blank nodes on a maxCount-1 property)
# with any example that happens to define that same id locally with its own geometry -- which
# several ids here do (see referenced-objects-CONFLICTS.md). A bare `a geojson:Feature` triple is
# deliberately the ONLY triple asserted for every id below -- it satisfies the SHACL existence
# check without asserting any cardinality-constrained property, so it can never collide with a
# richer definition of the same id defined independently elsewhere in the register (rdf:type is
# not cardinality-constrained; a duplicate `a geojson:Feature` triple from two sources just
# collapses to one in the merged graph).

<http://www.example.com/features/PC> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/PVE> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/PVS> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/Px1> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/Px2> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/Px3> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/Px4> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/Px5> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/arcP1> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/arcP2> a geojson:Feature .

<http://www.example.com/features/arcP3> a geojson:Feature .

