# uuid:ShellA / uuid:ShellB ARE defined inline in topo-feature-multi-collection's
# aggregate-solids.json `shells` array, but a separate pre-existing bug means array items in
# rings/faces/shells don't always get their own RDF subject asserted during JSON-LD uplift, so
# the Solid features that reference them by id can see them as dangling. Stubbed here as a
# workaround until that uplift bug is fixed at the source.
<uuid:ShellA> a geojson:Feature .

<uuid:ShellB> a geojson:Feature .

